Rem ==================================================================
Rem devils-dust-core.shoddy — Devil's Dust, the pure model.
Rem
Rem "Devil's dust" was the airborne fibre that filled a shoddy mill,
Rem thrown off by the devil — the toothed drum that tore rags back into
Rem wool. This models that air: a flock of wool wisps steered by the
Rem three classic boids rules (Reynolds 1987) — separation, alignment,
Rem cohesion — plus a fourth steering force, the draft rising off the
Rem devil. The flock is a value; each frame is a pure function of the
Rem last one. No mutation anywhere.
Rem
Rem Everything here is headless: the state records, the per-frame step,
Rem the steering arithmetic. It includes no scribbler, so test.shoddy
Rem exercises it without a window. devils-dust.shoddy adds the drawing,
Rem the event loop, and the tuning panel on top.
Rem
Rem The behavioural constants live in a Knobs record carried inside the
Rem Dust — NewKnobs() holds the defaults — so the panel can retune the
Rem storm while it blows. The knob TABLE (KnobId/KnobName/KnobLo/KnobHi/
Rem KnobGet/KnobSet) is the pure model of that panel: four tabs, each a
Rem few knobs, every value clamped to its rails. Only behaviour is a
Rem knob; the room's geometry stays fixed Defs below.
Rem
Rem Each wisp carries its own past as data — Trail is the last few
Rem positions, capped at TrailLen — so the renderer needs no framebuffer
Rem tricks to fade a streak. Loft is the wisp's buoyancy budget in
Rem frames: while it lasts the wisp rides the flock and the draft; when
Rem it runs out the wisp drops out of the flock and rains down where it
Rem is. Gravity (Settle) floats every falling wisp toward the floor at
Rem no more than FallMax; landed wool skids at FloorY until the sweep
Rem returns it to the devil. A wisp that leaves the world respawns at
Rem the devil's rim, flung up and out — and wool deep in the exit zones
Rem may be recycled a little early (RecycleP), so the drum spits a
Rem steady trickle rather than a burst each time a clump escapes.
Rem
Rem Alongside the wool rides the fine dust: Motes, a second population
Rem of single-pixel particles that drift on the draft without flocking
Rem (no O(n^2) for them) and wrap at the edges, so the air is never
Rem clear anywhere in the room.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "seq.shoddy"
Include "math.shoddy"

Rem ---- fixed geometry and grain --------------------------------------
Rem The room's geometry all hangs together: the floor strip sits at the
Rem bottom, wool rests just above it, and the devil stands mid-room on
Rem the floor — so resizing the world moves everything along with it.

Def WorldW() As Number
    1280
Def WorldH() As Number
    720
Def TrailLen() As Number
    5
Def FloorTop() As Number
    WorldH() - 22
Def FloorY() As Number
    FloorTop() - 7
Def DevilX() As Number
    WorldW() / 2
Def DevilY() As Number
    FloorTop() - 102
Def DrumR() As Number
    42
Def MoteFlutter() As Number
    0.02
Def MoteMin() As Number
    0.18
Def MoteMax() As Number
    0.84

Rem ---- the knobs -----------------------------------------------------
Rem Every behavioural tunable, one record. Constructor order matters —
Rem record fields are positional — so NewKnobs below lists them in the
Rem same order, tab by tab: LIFE, TEMPO, FLOCK, PACE.

Type Knobs
    LoftMin    As Number     Rem LIFE  1 - frames of buoyancy, at least
    LoftMax    As Number     Rem LIFE  2 - frames of buoyancy, at most
    Settle     As Number     Rem LIFE  3 - gravity
    LiftK      As Number     Rem LIFE  4 - devil updraft strength
    DraftR     As Number     Rem LIFE  5 - devil updraft reach
    MinSpeed   As Number     Rem TEMPO 1 - wisp speed floor
    MaxSpeed   As Number     Rem TEMPO 2 - wisp speed ceiling
    FallMax    As Number     Rem TEMPO 3 - terminal fall rate
    FlutterK   As Number     Rem TEMPO 4 - constant turbulence
    TumbleP    As Number     Rem TEMPO 5 - tumble chance per frame
    TumbleK    As Number     Rem TEMPO 6 - tumble kick size
    AlignK     As Number     Rem FLOCK 1 - match neighbour headings
    CohereK    As Number     Rem FLOCK 2 - drift to centre of mass
    SepK       As Number     Rem FLOCK 3 - personal-space push
    SepR       As Number     Rem FLOCK 4 - personal-space radius
    NeighborR  As Number     Rem FLOCK 5 - who counts as a neighbour
    SweepP     As Number     Rem PACE  1 - floor sweep chance per frame
    RecycleP   As Number     Rem PACE  2 - exit-zone recycle chance
    FiberCount As Number     Rem PACE  3 - wisps in the air
    MoteCount  As Number     Rem PACE  4 - specks in the haze
    DrumStep   As Number     Rem PACE  5 - drum spin, radians per frame

Rem The frozen defaults, in field order.
Def NewKnobs() As Knobs
    Knobs(240, 480, 0.035, 0.1, 260, 0.7, 3.1, 1.3, 0.12, 0.04, 0.9, 0.025, 0.003, 0.06, 16, 55, 0.02, 0.012, 100, 180, 0.264)

Rem Full stop: the machine goes dark. The drum winds to a standstill,
Rem the updraft dies, throws and tumbles cease, the sweep stops and
Rem nothing recycles — airborne wool loses its driver, settles under
Rem plain gravity, and lies where it lands. Loft at the rail minimum so
Rem any stray respawn drops almost at once. Every value sits legally on
Rem its rails; STOP is a lever position, not a cheat.
Def StopKnobs() As Knobs
    Knobs(30, 60, 0.035, 0, 260, 0, 1.2, 1.3, 0.01, 0, 0, 0.025, 0.003, 0.06, 16, 55, 0, 0, 100, 180, 0)

Rem The gentle end of the lever: every motion knob wound down to about
Rem a third — languid speeds, floaty gravity, a lazy drum, wool left
Rem lying on the floor — but the LOFT stays at the defaults, so the sky
Rem never empties. Slow wool is still flying wool.
Def SlowKnobs() As Knobs
    Knobs(240, 480, 0.012, 0.04, 260, 0.25, 1.1, 0.45, 0.04, 0.015, 0.3, 0.009, 0.001, 0.02, 16, 55, 0.006, 0.004, 100, 180, 0.09)

Rem True when two settings are the same lever position — the panel uses
Rem this to light the preset the goal currently sits on.
Def KnobsMatch(a As Knobs, b As Knobs) As Boolean
    All(Range(1, 21), Fn(i) => Abs(KnobGet(a, i) - KnobGet(b, i)) < 0.0001)

Rem Overloaded: a value meaningfully past its rail — reachable only
Rem through the ELEVEN lever, never by hand. The ignition point sits 8%
Rem past the rail (a third of eleven's 25% margin), and it is RELATIVE
Rem for a reason: the glide approaches a goal exponentially, so winding
Rem down from eleven the value hugs the rail from above — against an
Rem absolute epsilon the ember would smoulder for half a minute after
Rem the lever moved to MAX. At 8% it cools in a couple of seconds and
Rem ignites within one on the way up.
Def KnobHot(kb As Knobs, id As Number) As Boolean
    KnobGet(kb, id) > KnobHi(id) * 1.08

Rem Every knob at exactly its rail — the loudest setting the panel can
Rem reach by hand. This is ten.
Def MaxKnobs() As Knobs
    Knobs(KnobHi(1), KnobHi(2), KnobHi(3), KnobHi(4), KnobHi(5), KnobHi(6), KnobHi(7), KnobHi(8), KnobHi(9), KnobHi(10), KnobHi(11), KnobHi(12), KnobHi(13), KnobHi(14), KnobHi(15), KnobHi(16), KnobHi(17), KnobHi(18), KnobHi(19), KnobHi(20), KnobHi(21))

Rem These go to eleven. Every knob a full quarter past its rail —
Rem KnobSet clamps mere mortals at KnobHi, but this constructor doesn't
Rem go through the panel, so the values sit where no slider can reach
Rem and the gauges burn ember to say so. The two population counts stay
Rem whole.
Def ElevenKnobs() As Knobs
    Knobs(KnobHi(1) * 1.25, KnobHi(2) * 1.25, KnobHi(3) * 1.25, KnobHi(4) * 1.25, KnobHi(5) * 1.25, KnobHi(6) * 1.25, KnobHi(7) * 1.25, KnobHi(8) * 1.25, KnobHi(9) * 1.25, KnobHi(10) * 1.25, KnobHi(11) * 1.25, KnobHi(12) * 1.25, KnobHi(13) * 1.25, KnobHi(14) * 1.25, KnobHi(15) * 1.25, KnobHi(16) * 1.25, KnobHi(17) * 1.25, KnobHi(18) * 1.25, Round(KnobHi(19) * 1.25), Round(KnobHi(20) * 1.25), KnobHi(21) * 1.25)

Rem A population count mid-glide: whole, and never stalled. A rounded
Rem Lerp freezes once the remaining gap drops under 1/(2t) — the step
Rem rounds back to where it started and WISPS sits 20 short of its goal
Rem forever — so when rounding eats the step, the count moves by one
Rem anyway. One wisp a frame is a fine trickle for the last stretch.
Def WindCount(a As Number, b As Number, t As Number) As Number
    Let stepped = Round(Lerp(a, b, t))
    If t > 0 And stepped = a And a <> b Then
        a + Sgn(b - a)
    Else
        stepped

Rem Glide between two knob settings: an 1875 devil is tons of iron on a
Rem belt drive — it does not jump to a new speed, it winds there. A
Rem straight Lerp on every field, deliberately unclamped so a goal past
Rem the rails (ELEVEN) stays reachable; the population counts go
Rem through WindCount so they stay whole and always arrive.
Def BlendKnobs(a As Knobs, b As Knobs, t As Number) As Knobs
    Knobs(Lerp(LoftMin(a), LoftMin(b), t), Lerp(LoftMax(a), LoftMax(b), t), Lerp(Settle(a), Settle(b), t), Lerp(LiftK(a), LiftK(b), t), Lerp(DraftR(a), DraftR(b), t), Lerp(MinSpeed(a), MinSpeed(b), t), Lerp(MaxSpeed(a), MaxSpeed(b), t), Lerp(FallMax(a), FallMax(b), t), Lerp(FlutterK(a), FlutterK(b), t), Lerp(TumbleP(a), TumbleP(b), t), Lerp(TumbleK(a), TumbleK(b), t), Lerp(AlignK(a), AlignK(b), t), Lerp(CohereK(a), CohereK(b), t), Lerp(SepK(a), SepK(b), t), Lerp(SepR(a), SepR(b), t), Lerp(NeighborR(a), NeighborR(b), t), Lerp(SweepP(a), SweepP(b), t), Lerp(RecycleP(a), RecycleP(b), t), WindCount(FiberCount(a), FiberCount(b), t), WindCount(MoteCount(a), MoteCount(b), t), Lerp(DrumStep(a), DrumStep(b), t))

Rem ---- the knob table ------------------------------------------------
Rem The pure model of the tuning panel: knobs are numbered 1..21 in
Rem field order, arranged on four tabs. The window half only ever asks
Rem this table for names, rails, and values — it holds no knowledge of
Rem its own.

Def TabName(tab As Number) As String
    Select Case tab
        Case 1
            "LIFE"
        Case 2
            "TEMPO"
        Case 3
            "FLOCK"
        Case Else
            "PACE"

Def KnobRows(tab As Number) As Number
    Select Case tab
        Case 2
            6
        Case Else
            5

Rem Row r on tab t, as a knob id 1..21.
Def KnobId(tab As Number, row As Number) As Number
    Select Case tab
        Case 1
            row
        Case 2
            5 + row
        Case 3
            11 + row
        Case Else
            16 + row

Def KnobName(id As Number) As String
    Select Case id
        Case 1
            "LOFT MIN"
        Case 2
            "LOFT MAX"
        Case 3
            "GRAVITY"
        Case 4
            "LIFT"
        Case 5
            "DRAFT R"
        Case 6
            "MIN SPD"
        Case 7
            "MAX SPD"
        Case 8
            "FALL MAX"
        Case 9
            "FLUTTER"
        Case 10
            "TUMBLE P"
        Case 11
            "TUMBLE K"
        Case 12
            "ALIGN"
        Case 13
            "COHERE"
        Case 14
            "SEPARATE"
        Case 15
            "SEP R"
        Case 16
            "NEIGHBOR"
        Case 17
            "SWEEP"
        Case 18
            "RECYCLE"
        Case 19
            "WISPS"
        Case 20
            "MOTES"
        Case Else
            "SPIN"

Def KnobLo(id As Number) As Number
    Select Case id
        Case 1
            30
        Case 2
            60
        Case 3
            0
        Case 4
            0
        Case 5
            40
        Case 6
            0
        Case 7
            0.5
        Case 8
            0.2
        Case 9
            0
        Case 10
            0
        Case 11
            0
        Case 12
            0
        Case 13
            0
        Case 14
            0
        Case 15
            2
        Case 16
            10
        Case 17
            0
        Case 18
            0
        Case 19
            10
        Case 20
            0
        Case Else
            0

Def KnobHi(id As Number) As Number
    Select Case id
        Case 1
            900
        Case 2
            1200
        Case 3
            0.15
        Case 4
            0.3
        Case 5
            500
        Case 6
            1.6
        Case 7
            6
        Case 8
            3.5
        Case 9
            0.35
        Case 10
            0.2
        Case 11
            2.2
        Case 12
            0.1
        Case 13
            0.015
        Case 14
            0.22
        Case 15
            48
        Case 16
            150
        Case 17
            0.35
        Case 18
            0.06
        Case 19
            200
        Case 20
            350
        Case Else
            0.8

Def KnobGet(kb As Knobs, id As Number) As Number
    Select Case id
        Case 1
            LoftMin(kb)
        Case 2
            LoftMax(kb)
        Case 3
            Settle(kb)
        Case 4
            LiftK(kb)
        Case 5
            DraftR(kb)
        Case 6
            MinSpeed(kb)
        Case 7
            MaxSpeed(kb)
        Case 8
            FallMax(kb)
        Case 9
            FlutterK(kb)
        Case 10
            TumbleP(kb)
        Case 11
            TumbleK(kb)
        Case 12
            AlignK(kb)
        Case 13
            CohereK(kb)
        Case 14
            SepK(kb)
        Case 15
            SepR(kb)
        Case 16
            NeighborR(kb)
        Case 17
            SweepP(kb)
        Case 18
            RecycleP(kb)
        Case 19
            FiberCount(kb)
        Case 20
            MoteCount(kb)
        Case Else
            DrumStep(kb)

Rem Set knob id to v, clamped to its rails; the two population counts
Rem are kept whole.
Def KnobSet(kb As Knobs, id As Number, v As Number) As Knobs
    Let v2 = Ifte(id = 19 Or id = 20, Round(Clamp(v, KnobLo(id), KnobHi(id))), Clamp(v, KnobLo(id), KnobHi(id)))
    Select Case id
        Case 1
            With(kb, LoftMin = v2)
        Case 2
            With(kb, LoftMax = v2)
        Case 3
            With(kb, Settle = v2)
        Case 4
            With(kb, LiftK = v2)
        Case 5
            With(kb, DraftR = v2)
        Case 6
            With(kb, MinSpeed = v2)
        Case 7
            With(kb, MaxSpeed = v2)
        Case 8
            With(kb, FallMax = v2)
        Case 9
            With(kb, FlutterK = v2)
        Case 10
            With(kb, TumbleP = v2)
        Case 11
            With(kb, TumbleK = v2)
        Case 12
            With(kb, AlignK = v2)
        Case 13
            With(kb, CohereK = v2)
        Case 14
            With(kb, SepK = v2)
        Case 15
            With(kb, SepR = v2)
        Case 16
            With(kb, NeighborR = v2)
        Case 17
            With(kb, SweepP = v2)
        Case 18
            With(kb, RecycleP = v2)
        Case 19
            With(kb, FiberCount = v2)
        Case 20
            With(kb, MoteCount = v2)
        Case Else
            With(kb, DrumStep = v2)

Rem ---- state ---------------------------------------------------------

Rem A remembered position on a wisp's trail.
Type Knot
    Kx As Number
    Ky As Number

Rem A rag colour from the mixed stock; real shoddy was mottled because
Rem the rags were.
Type Dye
    Dr As Number
    Dg As Number
    Db As Number

Type Fiber
    Fx    As Number
    Fy    As Number
    Vx    As Number
    Vy    As Number
    Trail As List Of Knot
    Cr    As Number
    Cg    As Number
    Cb    As Number
    Loft  As Number          Rem frames of buoyancy left; spent wool rains down

Rem A speck of fine dust: position, drift, and a fixed grey brightness.
Rem Not Vx/Vy — those are Fiber accessors, and two types sharing
Rem accessor names is asking for trouble.
Type Mote
    Mx As Number
    My As Number
    Ux As Number
    Uy As Number
    Mb As Number

Type Dust
    Fibers As List Of Fiber
    Motes  As List Of Mote
    Whirl  As Number         Rem drum angle, radians; only the renderer reads it
    Tune   As Knobs          Rem the live knob settings the step runs on

Rem A steering force, or a velocity — any little 2-vector. Not "Vec":
Rem Vx/Vy are already Fiber accessors, and two types sharing accessor
Rem names is asking for trouble.
Type Gust
    Gx As Number
    Gy As Number

Def AddGust(a As Gust, b As Gust) As Gust
    Gust(Gx(a) + Gx(b), Gy(a) + Gy(b))

Rem ---- spawning ------------------------------------------------------

Rem Mostly pale wool, streaked with dulled madder, indigo and brown —
Rem the mixed rag stock that made shoddy cloth mottled.
Def Dyes() As List Of Dye
    { Dye(234, 228, 214), Dye(216, 208, 190), Dye(222, 216, 206), Dye(238, 232, 222), Dye(178, 172, 162), Dye(196, 188, 174), Dye(172, 98, 88), Dye(106, 112, 148), Dye(148, 120, 94), Dye(208, 196, 152) }

Rem A wisp flung off the devil's rim: spawned on the drum edge somewhere
Rem along the upper arc — left-leaning throws and right-leaning throws
Rem alike — velocity along the same angle, fresh trail, fresh loft.
Def RimFiber(kb As Knobs) As Fiber
    Let a = RandRange(-2.9, -0.24)
    Let sp = RandRange(2, 3.3)
    Let d = Pick(Dyes())
    Fiber(DevilX() + Cos(a) * (DrumR() + 3), DevilY() + Sin(a) * (DrumR() + 3), Cos(a) * sp, Sin(a) * sp, { }, Dr(d), Dg(d), Db(d), RandRange(LoftMin(kb), LoftMax(kb)))

Rem A wisp already adrift — the opening frame should look mid-storm,
Rem not like a machine warming up. Its loft is already part-spent, so
Rem the first rain starts within seconds.
Def SkyFiber() As Fiber
    Let a = RandRange(0, Tau())
    Let sp = RandRange(1, 2.3)
    Let d = Pick(Dyes())
    Fiber(RandRange(60, WorldW() - 40), RandRange(40, WorldH() - 270), Cos(a) * sp, Sin(a) * sp, { }, Dr(d), Dg(d), Db(d), RandRange(60, 300))

Rem A speck already anywhere in the room, barely moving, warm grey.
Def NewMote() As Mote
    Mote(RandRange(0, WorldW()), RandRange(20, FloorY() - 1), RandRange(-0.3, 0.4), RandRange(-0.2, 0.2), RandInt(60, 110))

Def NewDust() As Dust
    Let kb = NewKnobs()
    Dust(Map(Range(1, FiberCount(kb)), Fn(i) => SkyFiber()), Map(Range(1, MoteCount(kb)), Fn(i) => NewMote()), 0, kb)

Rem ---- steering ------------------------------------------------------
Rem The three Reynolds rules, each a Gust. Neighbors excludes the wisp
Rem itself by position — no identity exists on a value, and two wisps
Rem sharing an exact position is as good as one.

Def Neighbors(f As Fiber, flock As List Of Fiber, kb As Knobs) As List Of Fiber
    Filter(flock, Fn(n) => (Fx(n) <> Fx(f) Or Fy(n) <> Fy(f)) And Dist(Fx(f), Fy(f), Fx(n), Fy(n)) < NeighborR(kb))

Def SumBy(xs As List Of Fiber, sel As [ Fiber -- Number ]) As Number
    Fold(xs, 0, Fn(a, x) => a + Call(sel, x))

Rem Only meaningful on a non-empty list; the rules guard with IsEmpty.
Def AvgBy(xs As List Of Fiber, sel As [ Fiber -- Number ]) As Number
    SumBy(xs, sel) / Length(xs)

Rem Cohesion: drift toward the neighbours' centre of mass.
Def Cohere(f As Fiber, ns As List Of Fiber, kb As Knobs) As Gust
    If IsEmpty(ns) Then
        Gust(0, 0)
    Else
        Gust((AvgBy(ns, Fn(n) => Fx(n)) - Fx(f)) * CohereK(kb), (AvgBy(ns, Fn(n) => Fy(n)) - Fy(f)) * CohereK(kb))

Rem Alignment: match the neighbours' average heading.
Def Align(f As Fiber, ns As List Of Fiber, kb As Knobs) As Gust
    If IsEmpty(ns) Then
        Gust(0, 0)
    Else
        Gust((AvgBy(ns, Fn(n) => Vx(n)) - Vx(f)) * AlignK(kb), (AvgBy(ns, Fn(n) => Vy(n)) - Vy(f)) * AlignK(kb))

Rem Separation: push directly away from anyone closer than SepR.
Def Separate(f As Fiber, ns As List Of Fiber, kb As Knobs) As Gust
    Fold(ns, Gust(0, 0), Fn(g, n) => Ifte(Dist(Fx(f), Fy(f), Fx(n), Fy(n)) < SepR(kb), Gust(Gx(g) + (Fx(f) - Fx(n)) * SepK(kb), Gy(g) + (Fy(f) - Fy(n)) * SepK(kb)), g))

Rem The fourth force: the room's air. With the devil mid-room the air
Rem blows outward from the machine toward both walls (Sgn picks the
Rem side); real gravity (Settle) presses everything gently down; a
Rem strong updraft near the devil (full strength at the drum, gone by
Rem DraftR); a soft push off the ceiling. No push off the floor —
Rem wool is allowed to land, and StepFiber handles the rest. Both side
Rem edges stay open — wisps that escape respawn at the drum, which is
Rem the cycle of the mill.
Def Draft(f As Fiber, kb As Knobs) As Gust
    Let lift = Smoothstep(DraftR(kb), 0, Dist(Fx(f), Fy(f), DevilX(), DevilY()))
    Let ax = 0.014 * Sgn(Fx(f) - DevilX())
    Let ay = Settle(kb) - LiftK(kb) * lift + Ifte(Fy(f) < 40, 0.09, 0)
    Gust(ax, ay)

Rem Random turbulence so the wool flutters instead of gliding — and,
Rem with probability TumbleP a frame, a real tumble: a kick hard enough
Rem to bend the flight line. Cotton doesn't hold a heading the way a
Rem starling does.
Def Flutter(kb As Knobs) As Gust
    Let kick = Ifte(Chance(TumbleP(kb)), TumbleK(kb), 0)
    Gust(RandRange(-FlutterK(kb), FlutterK(kb)) + RandRange(-kick, kick), RandRange(-FlutterK(kb), FlutterK(kb)) + RandRange(-kick, kick))

Rem Clamp speed into [lo, hi] without changing heading — wool never
Rem stalls dead and never streaks like a bullet; motes use gentler bounds.
Def LimitSpeed(vx As Number, vy As Number, lo As Number, hi As Number) As Gust
    Let sp = Hypot(vx, vy)
    If sp < 0.0001 Then
        Gust(0, -lo)
    Else
        Let s2 = Clamp(sp, lo, hi)
        Gust(vx * s2 / sp, vy * s2 / sp)

Rem ---- the step ------------------------------------------------------

Def OffWorld(x As Number, y As Number) As Boolean
    x < -20 Or x > WorldW() + 20 Or y < -20 Or y > WorldH() + 20

Rem While a wisp has loft it flies the full flock — the three Reynolds
Rem rules, the draft, the flutter. When its loft runs out it drops out
Rem of the flock in the literal sense: no cohesion, no alignment, no
Rem updraft, no outward drift — just separation (fluff still does not
Rem interpenetrate), gravity, and flutter — so it rains down more or
Rem less where it is instead of being herded to a wall first.
Def FiberSteer(f As Fiber, ns As List Of Fiber, kb As Knobs) As Gust
    If Loft(f) <= 0 Then
        AddGust(AddGust(Separate(f, ns, kb), Gust(0, Settle(kb))), Flutter(kb))
    Else
        AddGust(AddGust(AddGust(AddGust(Cohere(f, ns, kb), Align(f, ns, kb)), Separate(f, ns, kb)), Draft(f, kb)), Flutter(kb))

Rem One wisp, one frame: steer (by loft), clamp the speed, move, spend
Rem a frame of loft, remember where it was. Falling is capped at
Rem FallMax — fluff has a terminal velocity, so it floats down rather
Rem than drops — and the floor stops it at FloorY, where it skids and
Rem bounces in the draft until the sweep (Chance(SweepP) per frame)
Rem carries it back to the devil. Off the world means back to the devil
Rem too, and wool deep in either exit zone near the side walls may go
Rem back early (Chance(RecycleP) per frame), which spreads the respawns
Rem out: a steady trickle off the drum instead of a burst each time a
Rem clump escapes together.
Def StepFiber(f As Fiber, flock As List Of Fiber, kb As Knobs) As Fiber
    Let ns = Neighbors(f, flock, kb)
    Let steer = FiberSteer(f, ns, kb)
    Let v = LimitSpeed(Vx(f) + Gx(steer), Vy(f) + Gy(steer), MinSpeed(kb), MaxSpeed(kb))
    Let vy = Min(Gy(v), FallMax(kb))
    Let nx = Fx(f) + Gx(v)
    Let ny = Min(Fy(f) + vy, FloorY())
    If OffWorld(nx, ny) Or ((nx < 160 Or nx > WorldW() - 160) And Chance(RecycleP(kb))) Or (ny >= FloorY() And Chance(SweepP(kb))) Then
        RimFiber(kb)
    Else
        Fiber(nx, ny, Gx(v), vy, Taken(Prepend(Knot(Fx(f), Fy(f)), Trail(f)), TrailLen()), Cr(f), Cg(f), Cb(f), Loft(f) - 1)

Rem One speck, one frame: ride the outward drift and the devil's
Rem updraft with a little flutter, then wrap — off one side is back in
Rem at the other, under the floor is back at the ceiling — so the fine
Rem dust stays spread through the whole room forever.
Def StepMote(m As Mote, kb As Knobs) As Mote
    Let lift = Smoothstep(DraftR(kb), 0, Dist(Mx(m), My(m), DevilX(), DevilY()))
    Let v = LimitSpeed(Ux(m) + 0.003 * Sgn(Mx(m) - DevilX()) + RandRange(-MoteFlutter(), MoteFlutter()), Uy(m) + 0.003 - 0.02 * lift + RandRange(-MoteFlutter(), MoteFlutter()), MoteMin(), MoteMax())
    Mote(Wrap(Mx(m) + Gx(v), WorldW()), 15 + Wrap(My(m) + Gy(v) - 15, FloorY() - 15), Gx(v), Gy(v), Mb(m))

Rem ---- population sizing ---------------------------------------------
Rem The WISPS and MOTES knobs resize the live populations: a deficit is
Rem made up with fresh spawns off the drum (a visible burst — good
Rem feedback), a surplus is trimmed. At the right size the list passes
Rem through untouched, so the common frame costs nothing extra.

Def SizeFlock(flock As List Of Fiber, kb As Knobs) As List Of Fiber
    Let want = FiberCount(kb)
    Let have = Length(flock)
    If have < want Then
        Concat(flock, Map(Range(1, want - have), Fn(i) => RimFiber(kb)))
    Else
        If have > want Then
            Taken(flock, want)
        Else
            flock

Def SizeMotes(motes As List Of Mote, kb As Knobs) As List Of Mote
    Let want = MoteCount(kb)
    Let have = Length(motes)
    If have < want Then
        Concat(motes, Map(Range(1, want - have), Fn(i) => NewMote()))
    Else
        If have > want Then
            Taken(motes, want)
        Else
            motes

Rem The whole room, one frame: size the populations to the knobs, then
Rem every wisp steps against the same previous flock — a pure function
Rem of the last frame's value, under the settings it carries.
Def Advance(d As Dust) As Dust
    Let kb = Tune(d)
    Let flock = SizeFlock(Fibers(d), kb)
    Dust(Map(flock, Fn(f) => StepFiber(f, flock, kb)), Map(SizeMotes(Motes(d), kb), Fn(m) => StepMote(m, kb)), Whirl(d) + DrumStep(kb), kb)

Rem ---- meters --------------------------------------------------------
Rem Read-only measurements of the storm, one cheap O(n) pass each —
Rem nothing here feeds back into the step. The footer readout draws
Rem these; the window half adds only the two meters that need memory
Rem across frames (measured FPS and smoothed throughput).

Rem Wool that has not landed. Landed wool sits pinned at FloorY, so the
Rem position alone decides.
Def Airborne(flock As List Of Fiber) As List Of Fiber
    Filter(flock, Fn(f) => Fy(f) < FloorY())

Rem The lifecycle census: riding the flock, raining down, or on the
Rem floor awaiting the sweep. Position outranks loft — grounded wool is
Rem LANDED even if a fresh gust could still lift it.
Type Census
    Aloft   As Number
    Raining As Number
    Landed  As Number

Def AddWisp(c As Census, f As Fiber) As Census
    If Fy(f) >= FloorY() Then
        With(c, Landed = Landed(c) + 1)
    Else
        If Loft(f) > 0 Then
            With(c, Aloft = Aloft(c) + 1)
        Else
            With(c, Raining = Raining(c) + 1)

Def TakeCensus(flock As List Of Fiber) As Census
    Fold(flock, Census(0, 0, 0), AddWisp)

Rem Polarization, the classic flocking order parameter: |mean velocity|
Rem over mean speed of the airborne wool. 1 means everyone flies the
Rem same way (starlings); near 0 means incoherent drift (cotton).
Def OrderParam(flock As List Of Fiber) As Number
    Let air = Airborne(flock)
    If IsEmpty(air) Then
        0
    Else
        Let sx = SumBy(air, Fn(f) => Vx(f))
        Let sy = SumBy(air, Fn(f) => Vy(f))
        Let sp = SumBy(air, Fn(f) => Hypot(Vx(f), Vy(f)))
        If sp < 0.0001 Then
            0
        Else
            Hypot(sx, sy) / sp

Rem Mean speed of the airborne wool.
Def MeanSpeed(flock As List Of Fiber) As Number
    Let air = Airborne(flock)
    If IsEmpty(air) Then
        0
    Else
        SumBy(air, Fn(f) => Hypot(Vx(f), Vy(f))) / Length(air)

Rem Mean height of the airborne wool above the floor, in pixels.
Def Altitude(flock As List Of Fiber) As Number
    Let air = Airborne(flock)
    If IsEmpty(air) Then
        0
    Else
        SumBy(air, Fn(f) => FloorY() - Fy(f)) / Length(air)

Rem Wool that went through the devil this frame: a respawn starts with
Rem an empty trail, so no extra bookkeeping is needed to spot one.
Def FreshCount(flock As List Of Fiber) As Number
    CountIf(flock, Fn(f) => IsEmpty(Trail(f)))
